  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A circular coil of 1000 turns each with area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is rotated about its vertical diameter at the rate of one revolution per second in a uniform horizontal magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The maximum voltage generation will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "440",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p><p>The maximum emf generated is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p><p>Thus, maximum emf is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>439</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>440</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p>",
